From: Kestrel OS port <local>
Subject: [PATCH, DIAGNOSTIC, LOCAL-ONLY] drop SCM interconnects on Slim 3

Rationale: firmware:scm's icc path (aggre2 + mc_virt) never resolves,
so SCM defers forever; the X1E PDC quirk hard-requires SCM
(qcom-pdc.c: `if (!qcom_scm_is_available()) return -EPROBE_DEFER`),
and TLMM (wakeup-parent = PDC), GPIO, USB PHYs and USB storage hang
behind it to a black Hang at ~19s. devm_of_icc_get treats a missing
property as no-vote, so SCM probes without bus voting. NOT for
publication or general ARM64 support.

---
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/x126100-lenovo-ideapad-slim3.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/x126100-lenovo-ideapad-slim3.dts
@@ -1720,3 +1720,14 @@
 &mdss_dp2_phy { status = "disabled"; };
 &mdss_dp3_phy { status = "disabled"; };
 &ufs_mem_phy { status = "disabled"; };
+
+/* DIAGNOSTIC 2026-10-15 (0009): delete firmware:scm interconnects.
+ * SCM's icc path (aggre2 + mc_virt) never resolves on this machine,
+ * so SCM defers forever; the X1E PDC quirk hard-requires SCM, and
+ * TLMM (wakeup-parent PDC), GPIO, USB PHYs and USB storage hang
+ * behind it. devm_of_icc_get treats a missing property as no-vote
+ * (NULL path), so SCM probes without bus voting. Local-only, not
+ * for publication. */
+&scm {
+	/delete-property/ interconnects;
+};
